The portable C in the scenario start-screen: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/start-screen.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 10 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the second of the two lines that ask for Enter on a screen of 40
columns names the program, two letters shorter, and the cursor is behind it;
on a screen of graphics the one line is dots, which show here as cells,
other dots for another name and two letters fewer of them. And the box of
F10 names the program in its title and in its question, by a name that is
two letters shorter: the box is two cells narrower, a cell on either side,
and its shadow ends a cell further left

